From 28a9aac9190ede72f98bbdca62ae1cc745467da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wjxn13 <236573882+wjxn13@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:04:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] feat(core): broadcast a leading run of mentions to
 every named agent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"@wb @dsh 看下这个" used to reach only wb: the gate read the FIRST
mention and dropped the message for everyone else. Users brief several
agents at once by writing their names in a row, and every one of them
should answer.

New two-step rule in mentionGateTargets (engine.go):

1. A contiguous run of @names at the very start of the message (separated
   only by whitespace, commas, ideographic commas, semicolons, + or &)
   addresses ALL of them; every hit goes into the owner set, deduped and
   in written order. scanLeadingMentionRun stops at the first character
   that is neither a separator nor another alias, so the @dsh inside
   "@claude 帮我叫 @dsh 干活" stays out of the run; a bare @ ends it.
2. Otherwise the previous positional rule applies unchanged.

MentionSticky grows from one name into a set: Mark takes variadic
projects (dedup, REPLACE not merge — a later single @ narrows the set),
Lookup returns a copy of the slice. The photo after "@wb @dsh 看下这张图"
belongs to both of them.

mentionGateDrop becomes a thin wrapper joining the owners with "," so
existing tests and the drop-log format stay stable; mentionsSelf now
DELEGATES to mentionGateTargets so the stickiness marker and the gate
can never diverge; rememberAddressee becomes rememberAddressees and
mediaRouteOwner resolves a whole owner set.
